  "name": "Death Wink",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/unholy/beam-ringed-impact-purple.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>At 5th level, you gain a new attack option which can be performed by winking. This attack can be used to replace any of your unarmed strikes, including a flurry of blows and the martial arts bonus action attack, and counts as an aesthetic weapon.</p>\n<p>This special attack is a ranged weapon attack with a range of 30 feet. You are proficient with it, and you add your Dexterity modifier to its attack and damage rolls. Its damage is bludgeoning, and its damage die is a d6. This die changes as you gain brawler levels, as shown in the Martial Arts column of the Brawler table.</p>\n<p>Once per turn, the first creature you hit with this attack must make a Strength Saving throw against your Spirit DC. On a failure, they are either pushed back 10ft or knocked prone (the user's choice).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
